Engine: the Hall of Fame's entries on the wire, "HOFM" (open fix 50).

STATUS: APPLIED 29 September 2026 by work order 188 (Part 6, the Hall of
Fame in HD), under the order's advance approval of the engine fixes a part
needs ("Engine fixes: approved in advance for this run") — orion2re
65b41b66 on orionlayer-local (before: 6859e163), this file's diff byte for
byte (index lines included). Required by tools/version_check.py since work
order 188.

PROOF ON THE TIP IT WAS APPLIED TO (work order 188): in a scratch clone of
orionlayer-local at 6859e163 this file applied with `patch -p1 --dry-run`
and `patch -p1`, no offset, no fuzz, the applied tree's diff equal to it;
ext_api.cpp and score.cpp compiled alone with the build's own command
(-fsyntax-only), exit 0; two controls were refused by the compiler, exit 1
each — `SCORE::_entry_to_flash` misspelt `_entry_to_flsh` in ext_api.cpp,
`ext::g_hof_live` misspelt `g_hof_liv` in score.cpp. Then applied to
~/orion2re (no offset), built (ninja, no error) and committed.

To revert, from ~/orion2re on the orionlayer-local branch: `git revert
65b41b66` or `patch -R -p1`; then rebuild. See the entry,
doc/orion2re_open_fixes.md 50.

WIRE LAYOUT — "HOFM", written LAST, while 14 is reported and the screen
takes input: uint8 version 1, int16 the file's version (0x82), int16 the
flashed entry (-1 none), uint8 count (10), then per row in the display
order: int16 record, int16 score, int16 race id, uint8 difficulty, and three
strings each uint8 length + raw bytes — the player's name, the race's name,
the difficulty's word as the engine loaded it.

WHAT IT IS FOR
SCORE::Hall_Of_Fame_Screen_ draws its ten entries from SCORE::_hof (HOF.M2)
in the order Init sorted them and the difficulty words from ESTRINGS; none
of it was serialized, and the game-end way in runs it under the return
screen's id. HD cannot read HOF.M2 itself (decision 60's reasoning: the
engine may rewrite the file on entry, HD's folder need not be the game's,
the words are the engine's). The patch reports 14 on both ways in and puts
the table on the wire while the screen takes input — in the display order,
each entry's record, score, race id, difficulty and its word, the player's
and the race's names — with the entry the screen flashes.

diff --git a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
index 03b33614..5881e870 100644
--- a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
+++ b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
@@ -1089,6 +1089,46 @@ static void SerializeState(std::vector<uint8_t>& buf,
             Write16(buf, COMBFIND::_target.num_player_targets);
         }
     }
+
+    // 17. The Hall of Fame: "HOFM", written ONLY while it takes input (it
+    //     reports 14 on both ways in), and LAST. OrionLayer, open fix 50.
+    //
+    //     SCORE::Hall_Of_Fame_Screen_ draws its ten entries from SCORE::_hof
+    //     in the order Init sorted them (_hi->sort_list, score descending)
+    //     and the difficulty words from ESTRINGS into _difficulty_string —
+    //     none of it was serialized. Sent in the DISPLAY order, as the file
+    //     holds it: the record, the score, the race id, the difficulty and
+    //     its word as the engine loaded it, the player's and the race's
+    //     names; and the entry the screen flashes (a new record at game end).
+    if (current_screen == SCREEN_HALL_OF_FAME && g_hof_live && SCORE::_hi != nullptr) {
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'H');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'O');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'F');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'M');
+        Write8(buf, 1);                                   // block version
+        Write16(buf, SCORE::_hof.version);
+        Write16(buf, SCORE::_entry_to_flash);
+        Write8(buf, 10);
+        for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
+            const int16_t r = SCORE::_hi->sort_list[i][1];
+            const bool ok = r >= 0 && r < 10;
+            Write16(buf, r);
+            Write16(buf, ok ? SCORE::_hof.scores[r] : 0);
+            Write16(buf, ok ? SCORE::_hof.race_ids[r] : 0);
+            const int8_t d = ok ? SCORE::_hof.difficulties[r] : 0;
+            Write8(buf, (uint8_t)d);
+            const char* strs[3] = {
+                ok ? SCORE::_hof.player_names[r] : "",
+                ok ? SCORE::_hof.race_names[r] : "",
+                (d >= 0 && d < GAME_DIFFICULTY_COUNT) ? SCORE::_difficulty_string[d] : ""};
+            const size_t caps[3] = {20, 20, 15};
+            for (int k = 0; k < 3; k++) {
+                const size_t len = strnlen(strs[k], caps[k]);
+                Write8(buf, (uint8_t)len);
+                WriteBytes(buf, strs[k], len);
+            }
+        }
+    }
 }
 
